  The Tsurugi is a two-handed weapon: no twoweaponing, danger of getting
it cursed..  I wouldn't bother with it.  

  Firebrand destroys potions, scrolls and spellbooks.  It's also just an
ordinary long sword against fire-resistant monsters.  

  Sunsword's nice if you make use of the light source.  Better to use
lamps/lanterns when appropriate.  They have a larger light circle in any
case.  Sunsword prevents blinding from any light source.  Probably not
Archons.  Sunsword does extra damage against undead, otherwise does
normal long sword damage.


  Snickersnee does an average extra 4.5 damage to all monsters. 

Excalibur
  (lawful long sword)
  Wielded
    +d5 to hit and +d10 damage to all monsters.
    Confers level drain resistance and automatic searching.
    Manual and automatic searching is more likely to succeed.
    Even eyeless monsters will be able to locate you.
    Demon princes will be generated hostile.


  That +d10 damage to all monsters averages to 5.5 extra damage.
Even better than Snickersnee.  Level drain resistance is nice to have.
Automatic searching won't really help unless you move slowly enough
to make use of it.  (I don't.)

  Hostile demon princes will be handled by your secondary silver saber.
+10.5 extra damage to demons, etc.  Bless it and Excalibur and they'll
do a total of 4 more damage to demons, etc.

